  "prefLabel": "Plc 1001.02 Applicability",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1001.02 Applicability.\n\n(a) Plc 1001 shall apply to persons seeking the service(s) identified in the section that establishes the fee.\n\n(b) Plc 1002 shall apply to applicants who apply for the type of license identified in the section that establishes the fee.\n\n(c) Plc 1003 shall apply to board members who seek per diems for attending board meetings and undertaking other board-related business or who seek reimbursement for expenses related to the same, as identified in the section that establishes the procedures.\n\n(d) Plc 1004 shall apply to applicants for licensing in a profession for which an examination is required, as identified in the section that establishes the fee.\n\n(e) Based on the authority conferred on the executive director by RSA 310:5, I, the fees established in this chapter shall supersede any corresponding fees established in any supported board’s rule.\n\nSource. #13264, INTERIM, eff 9-22-21; ss by #13336, eff 1-27-22; ss by #13838, eff 1-26-24; ss by #14289, eff 7-1-25, EXPIRES: 7-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1000.html"
